# mcpb pack always excludes .git, .DS_Store, *.mcpb and a handful of JS-tooling files
# (see @anthropic-ai/mcpb's built-in EXCLUDE_PATTERNS). build.sh stages only manifest.json,
# pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md, LICENSE and src/ into the packed directory -- nothing
# below should ever actually match today. These patterns are defense-in-depth against a
# future staging change that copies more than intended (a stray checked-out .venv/, a
# __pycache__/ from running tests locally, etc).
#
# F06: a bare `*.dist-info/RECORD` (no `**/` prefix) is anchored to the top level under the
# `ignore` package's gitignore semantics and never matches a nested path -- 71 nested RECORD
# files shipped in the vendored bundle this replaced. Every pattern here that names a
# directory is written `**/<name>/` so it matches at any depth, not just the bundle root.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.dist-info/
.venv/
tests/
dist/
analysis/
docs/
.github/
